# Miniforge.ai Header & Copyright

<version>2.0.0</version>

## Scope — OSS repositories only

**This rule applies exclusively to Apache-2.0 licensed (open source) repositories.**

Detection: the repository root must contain a `LICENSE` file whose content includes the string `"Apache"`. If no such file exists, or the file contains `"Proprietary"` / `"All Rights Reserved"`, **do not apply this rule**.

> **Why `remediation.strategy: manual` and `autoFixable: false`:** two independent reasons, both blocking.
>
> 1. The Apache-license gate above is a human-judgement check that cannot be encoded in the frontmatter's `detection.*` fields. An automated runner must not prepend a copyright block without confirming the target is an OSS repo.
> 2. **The frontmatter format cannot express this template.** Quoted scalars are read literally — no escape processing, and no block-scalar (`|`) syntax. The `\n` sequences in `remediation.template` below stay as a literal backslash and `n`; they never become newlines. A `mechanical` prepend would therefore write the entire header as one line of literal `\n` characters, and because that line does contain both `Christopher Lester` and the email address, `detection` would then report the file **compliant**. The result is silent corruption that satisfies its own gate.
>
> The template below is retained as the canonical block to copy **by hand**, not as a machine-applicable patch. Do not set `strategy: mechanical` or `autoFixable: true` on this rule until the format can represent a multi-line literal.
>
> **Why `*.md` is not in the globs:** Root-level markdown files such as `CLAUDE.md`, `agents.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`, and `SECURITY.md` are structural files, not published content. The `docs/` and `specs/` globs cover the content directories where published articles live.

Proprietary Thesium products use `standards/thesium/project/header-proprietary` instead. Never apply an Apache 2.0 copyright header to a proprietary file.

## Context
- Use when authoring or editing site, docs, blog, or README content in an Apache-licensed repo.

## Requirements
- Include this header block verbatim at the top of content.
- Use copyright owner: Christopher Lester (christopher@miniforge.ai).
- Do not attribute copyright to Miniforge.ai as an entity. ✅

